# MAGIC ## A. Developer Tools for Local Development

# COMMAND ----------

# MAGIC %md-sandbox
# MAGIC ### A1. Developer Tools Overview
# MAGIC
# MAGIC Three tools bring Databricks into local development from VS Code. Each is suited to a different kind of work.
# MAGIC <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr 1fr;gap:24px;max-width:1150px;margin:0 auto;font-family:sans-serif;align-items:start;">
# MAGIC   <div style="border-top:4px solid #4299E0;padding-top:14px;">
# MAGIC   <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:10px;height:52px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="terminal" style="height:44px;vertical-align:middle;"/></div>
# MAGIC   <div style="font-size:15pt;font-weight:700;color:#0b2026;text-align:center;margin-bottom:12px;">Databricks CLI</div>
# MAGIC   <ul style="font-size:12.5pt;color:#0b2026;padding-left:20px;margin:0;line-height:1.5;"><li>Ideal for <b>shell scripting</b> &amp; lightweight command-line tasks</li><li>Useful in development and CI/CD processes</li><li>Supports unified authentication (OAuth, PATs, etc.)</li><li>More interactive debugging compared to Notebooks</li></ul>
# MAGIC </div>
# MAGIC   <div style="border-top:4px solid #00A972;padding-top:14px;">
# MAGIC   <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:10px;height:52px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="databricks" style="height:44px;vertical-align:middle;"/></div>
# MAGIC   <div style="font-size:15pt;font-weight:700;color:#0b2026;text-align:center;margin-bottom:12px;">Databricks Connect V2</div>
# MAGIC   <ul style="font-size:12.5pt;color:#0b2026;padding-left:20px;margin:0;line-height:1.5;"><li>Runs Apache Spark code <b>remotely</b> on a Databricks cluster from a local environment</li><li>Ideal for interactive debugging and remote Spark job execution</li><li>Easy setup with <code>pip install databricks-connect&gt;=</code> your version</li></ul>
# MAGIC </div>
# MAGIC   <div style="border-top:4px solid #FFAB00;padding-top:14px;">
# MAGIC   <div style="text-align:center;margin-bottom:10px;height:52px;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;"><span style="display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;"><img src="data:image/png;base64," alt="databricks" style="height:44px;vertical-align:middle;"/><svg width="26" height="26" viewBox="0 0 100 100" style="vertical-align:middle;"><path d="M75 8 L95 18 V82 L75 92 L30 55 L12 70 L5 66 V34 L12 30 L30 45 Z M75 30 L48 50 L75 70 Z" fill="#3B82C4"/></svg></span></div>
# MAGIC   <div style="font-size:15pt;font-weight:700;color:#0b2026;text-align:center;margin-bottom:12px;">Databricks VS Code Extension</div>
# MAGIC   <ul style="font-size:12.5pt;color:#0b2026;padding-left:20px;margin:0;line-height:1.5;"><li>Integrates Databricks into VS Code for batch and interactive development</li><li>Simplifies setup with resource explorers and Databricks CLI</li><li>Supports running and debugging Python files on Databricks clusters</li><li>Keeps developers within VS Code, and provides <b>DAB features</b></li></ul>
# MAGIC </div>
# MAGIC </div>
# MAGIC
# MAGIC ##### Additional notes
# MAGIC
# MAGIC <details>
# MAGIC
# MAGIC - For many developers, an IDE like VS Code is the preferred choice &mdash; you can interact with Databricks in multiple ways while staying in the IDE, avoiding a switch to the Databricks browser UI.
# MAGIC - The <b>Databricks CLI</b> allows quick interactions through the command line. It is ideal for shell scripting and lightweight command-line tasks, useful in development and CI/CD processes, supports unified authentication (OAuth, PATs, etc.), and offers more interactive debugging compared to Notebooks.
# MAGIC - <b>Databricks Connect V2</b> runs Apache Spark code remotely on a Databricks cluster from a local environment. It is ideal for interactive debugging and remote Spark job execution, with an easy setup: `pip install databricks-connect>=<your version>`.
# MAGIC - The <b>Databricks VS Code Extension</b> integrates Databricks into VS Code for batch and interactive development, simplifies setup with resource explorers and the Databricks CLI, supports running and debugging Python files on clusters, and keeps developers within VS Code while providing DAB features.
# MAGIC
# MAGIC </details>

